invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_cpu writes the low byte of the session's
  description of the CPU and not the byte above it, so no traffic key
  records CH_CPU_AVX512 and AES-GCM never runs the 512-bit kernel, whatever
  the caller stated. The bytes are the same. bin/aes_runtime_test requires
  the key's second cpu byte to hold the value's after the call.

--- old
    k->key.cpu = (uint8_t)cpu;
    k->key.cpu_high = (uint8_t)(cpu >> 8);
}
--- new
    k->key.cpu = (uint8_t)cpu;
}
